{#
    One navigation list, wherever it is being drawn.

    The rail draws it twice — the main group and the tools group — and the
    narrow screen's More sheet draws it once more. All three are the same
    markup over lists `NavigationService` has already decided, so a change to
    how a navigation item looks is one edit rather than three that drift.

    `links`   the list of NavLink to draw
    `badges`  counts to show beside items, keyed by the item's id (optional)

    A list and not a landmark: whoever includes this owns the `<nav>` around it,
    because the sheet's list sits inside the tab bar's own and nesting one
    navigation landmark in another tells a screen reader there are two.

    The icon is server-rendered from the sprite (see `icon()`), and hidden from
    assistive technology: what says where the link goes is the text beside it.
    A badge's number is followed by a hidden word, so "Subscriptions 12" is
    read as twelve active subscriptions rather than a bare number.
#}
{% set badges = badges|default({}) %}
<ul class="nav-list">
    {% for link in links %}
        <li>
            <a class="nav-link{{ link.active ? ' is-active' : '' }}"
               href="{{ link.href }}"
               {{ link.active ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>
                {{ icon(link.icon, 'nav-icon') }}
                <span class="nav-label">{{ t(link.labelKey) }}</span>
                {% if badges[link.id] is defined %}
                    <span class="nav-badge num">{{ badges[link.id]|decimal(0) }}<span class="visually-hidden"> {{ t('shell.badge_active') }}</span></span>
                {% endif %}
            </a>
        </li>
    {% endfor %}
</ul>
